e, the purification of a compound is independent of:"}, "options": [{"id": "b83f60", "text": "Mobility or flow of solvent system", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262315"}, {"id": "82db72", "text": "Solubility of the compound", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262316"}, {"id": "4732b1", "text": "Length of the column or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>TLC</mi></math> Plate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262317"}, {"id": "ecc71d", "text": "Physical state of the pure compound", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262318"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262319", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e56814499d1e49588fa3a9"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa396"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements.<br />Statement I : The dipole moment of $\\stackrel{4}{\\mathrm{CH}_3}-\\stackrel{3~~~~}{\\mathrm{CH}}=\\stackrel{3~~~~}{\\mathrm{CH}}-\\stackrel{1~~~~}{\\mathrm{CH}}=\\mathrm{O}$ is greater than $\\stackrel{4}{\\mathrm{CH}_3}-\\stackrel{3}{\\mathrm{CH}_2}-\\stackrel{2}{\\mathrm{CH}_2}-\\stackrel{1}{\\mathrm{CH}}=\\mathrm{O}$<br />Statement II : $\\mathbf{C}_1-\\mathbf{C}_2$ bond length of $\\underset{4}{\\mathrm{CH}_3-\\mathrm{}} \\underset{3}{\\mathrm{CH=}} \\underset{2}{\\mathrm{CH}}-\\mathrm{CH}=\\mathrm{O}$ is greater than $\\mathrm{C}_1-\\mathrm{C}_2$ bond length of <img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FppGhHNzCMzpZPK9vKTS-0Mh_s55sA07kjWQ86lM0Dwc.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br />In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "e1fe6c", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d926231a"}, {"id": "33fb64", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d926231b"}, {"id": "1a7fda", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d926231c"}, {"id": "be3099", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d926231d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d926231e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4787"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ef8"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements.</p><p>Statement I : The compound&nbsp;<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F84d1f868-a11b-4068-978f-0cfd4ab0e59c-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 105px; height: 180px;\" />&nbsp;is&nbsp;optically active.</p><p>Statement II :&nbsp;<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7abc870f-925b-4752-890c-7311a5789806-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 169px; height: 145px;\" />​​​​​​​&nbsp;is mirror image of&nbsp;above compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statement, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "bd7aed", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d926231f"}, {"id": "88f11f", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262320"}, {"id": "16a26d", "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262321"}, {"id": "e37391", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262322"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f492ee0e063d9262323", "type": "singleCorrect", "